From 3eb2311f466371222ba0ceee5fa09bb5832aba8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 18:42:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05931/11362] [outer-loop] add native_gguf_backend_bisect
 substrate; exp5323 resolves the multi-milestone llama-cli blocker

User asked to dig into exp5323, the flag-bisect task I'd been watching
for after documenting the native llama-cli hang fix. Genuinely good
news: the conductor independently bisected to the same -st/--single-turn
fix, confirming completed_load_first_token_and_8_tokens=True with
authenticated GPU offload (backend_variant=llama-cli-single-turn-batch512)
-- resolving the blocker that stalled .484's exp5297 and .485's exp5309
across two milestones. runtime_unblocked_min_one_mandated=True,
sota_backend_candidate_ready=True.

It still got flagged DURATION_TOO_SHORT (20.8s) under the generic 60s
live_llm_inference floor -- the seventh time this exact substrate-
recognition bug class has appeared this week. A bisect that stops at
the first working flag combination (real GPU-backed model load, but not
a full generation benchmark across every variant) is genuinely faster
than the 60s floor is calibrated for.

Added local_native_llama_cpp_gguf_backend_bisect as the 9th recognized
substrate (5.0s floor), wired ahead of the generic live_llm_inference
check. Confirmed the earlier uppercase-MODEL_SPECS-casing fix (from
exp5262/exp5263 earlier this week) already covers this artifact's
methodology check -- 0 flags on live re-check, no further exemption
needed.

7 new tests (tests/python/test_adversarial_verify_native_gguf_backend_
bisect_substrate.py): recognition-function coverage, floor-value check,
an exact exp5323 reproduction now clean, a fabricated-near-instant-claim
regression guard, and a full-generation-still-needs-60s regression
guard. Full suite (298 tests) green. Corpus-wide dry-run sanity check
stable (5 qualifying artifacts, normal drift).

Un-quarantined exp5323: 0 flags (was 1 CRITICAL).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
